    "result_text": "The change is complete and verified green. Here's what I did.\n\n## Summary\n\nConsolidated the three separate owner duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) into a single derived `identityKey` = `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + householdId`, rejecting with 409 only on a **whole-key** match, and now return `identityKey` on the owner.\n\n### Key behaviour\n- `identityKey` is derived, not stored. `normalizedTelephone` is E.164 form, `email` is lower-cased/trimmed (empty when absent), `householdId` is the shared household id (empty when the owner isn't in a shared household \u2014 i.e. no `sharesHousehold: true`).\n- Because telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household with different telephones now have different keys and are **both allowed** \u2014 a deliberate behaviour change from the old household check. Only an exact full-key collision is a duplicate.\n\n### Files added\n- `function/owner/OwnerIdentity.java` \u2014 derives the key (`of(owner)`, `key(...)`) and the shared `householdIdFor(lastName, address)`; single source of the normalization + SHA-256 household hash.\n- `function/owner/CheckIdentityUnique.java` \u2014 the one check; computes the new owner's prospective key (using `sharesHousehold ? householdIdFor(...) : \"\"`) and compares against every existing owner's `OwnerIdentity.of(...)`.\n- `escalation/DuplicateIdentityException.java` + `...Handler.java` (409, body `{\"errors\":[\"identityKey\"]}`) and its escalation YAML.\n\n### Files changed\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 replaced the `checkTelephone \u2192 checkEmail \u2192 checkHousehold` steps with a single `checkIdentity` step.\n- `AssignHousehold.java` \u2014 refactored to reuse `OwnerIdentity.householdIdFor(...)` (same deterministic id), javadoc updated.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` property to the `Owner` schema.\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 populates `identityKey` via `OwnerIdentity.of(owner)`.\n\n### Files removed\nThe three old check functions, their three exceptions + handlers, and their three escalation YAMLs.\n\n### Verification\n`./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (`AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsIdentityCollision` passes: a second owner reusing another's telephone is rejected 409). Confirmed the generated `OwnerDto` now carries `identityKey` and no references to the removed classes remain.",
